1
00:00:27,527 --> 00:00:30,948
THE HUSBAND

2
00:00:35,202 --> 00:00:36,410
THIS SERIES IS FICTITIOUS

3
00:00:36,411 --> 00:00:39,039
CHILDREN WERE FILMED SAFELY
GEN AI WAS USED IN SELECT SCENES

4
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:44,211
EPISODE 10

5
00:01:43,145 --> 00:01:44,228
Let's go.

6
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,563
Yeah, I'm coming.

7
00:01:45,564 --> 00:01:46,606
I made the reservation.

8
00:01:47,691 --> 00:01:48,774
Soju or beer?

9
00:01:48,775 --> 00:01:50,985
-  Let's have both.
-  Yeah, I don't know about that.

10
00:01:50,986 --> 00:01:52,195
Drink it all.

11
00:02:03,165 --> 00:02:06,960
JI COMPUTER

12
00:02:17,971 --> 00:02:19,306
Good evening.

13
00:03:05,477 --> 00:03:07,061
Hello.

14
00:03:07,062 --> 00:03:08,730
Sir? Excuse me.

15
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:11,232
- Just a minute. Hi.
- Oh, hi.

16
00:03:14,152 --> 00:03:15,821
- Hi, there.
-  Hi.

17
00:03:16,571 --> 00:03:18,239
Hey, wait. Hold on.

18
00:03:18,240 --> 00:03:20,616
We've been neighbors for a while now.

19
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:24,830
I see you all the time, but I don't think
we've ever properly introduced ourselves.

20
00:03:25,497 --> 00:03:30,502
You see, I run a little
hair salon down the alley.

21
00:03:31,753 --> 00:03:33,255
Right next to the chicken place.

22
00:03:34,256 --> 00:03:35,424
Right.

23
00:03:35,924 --> 00:03:38,385
- You know, down the alley…
- Yeah. Okay.

24
00:03:39,094 --> 00:03:41,011
Come by when you need a haircut.

25
00:03:41,012 --> 00:03:42,180
Okay.

26
00:03:43,515 --> 00:03:45,516
Hey, I'm really sorry.

27
00:03:45,517 --> 00:03:48,477
Well, you look great now,

28
00:03:48,478 --> 00:03:51,522
but if you got
just a tiny little trim on your bangs,

29
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:53,733
you'd look so much better.

30
00:03:54,317 --> 00:03:55,735
- Drop by sometime.
- Okay.

31
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,321
Uh, wait, hold up.

32
00:03:58,905 --> 00:04:01,949
I don't think I can finish
all of this on my own.

33
00:04:01,950 --> 00:04:04,493
- Here, take this. Wait a minute.
- Okay.

34
00:04:04,494 --> 00:04:05,495
Oh, my gosh!

35
00:04:06,496 --> 00:04:07,705
Take this one instead.

36
00:04:07,706 --> 00:04:08,748
Hey, wait.

37
00:04:10,917 --> 00:04:13,169
Come by for a haircut sometime!

38
00:04:13,170 --> 00:04:14,212
Okay.

39
00:04:15,714 --> 00:04:17,382
He's cute.

40
00:04:54,586 --> 00:04:55,879
Kim Gyeongae!

41
00:04:56,505 --> 00:04:57,714
Open up.

42
00:04:59,007 --> 00:05:00,258
I know you're in there.

43
00:05:01,218 --> 00:05:02,552
Come on.

44
00:05:03,637 --> 00:05:06,848
I know your lights were on until just now.
Open up while I'm being nice.

45
00:05:09,518 --> 00:05:11,019
I'm not leaving empty-handed.

46
00:05:12,896 --> 00:05:13,980
Come out already!

47
00:05:14,773 --> 00:05:16,942
You better open up
before I kick the door down.

48
00:05:17,818 --> 00:05:20,278
Or I'm going to kill you.

49
00:05:21,988 --> 00:05:22,989
One.

50
00:05:23,532 --> 00:05:25,492
Two!

51
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:29,162
Look who it is. There you are.

52
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:32,707
You can't just show up like this
in the middle of the night.

53
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:36,001
I know you made money today.
Hand it over.

54
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:37,920
You just took all of it
a few days ago.

55
00:05:37,921 --> 00:05:39,338
I don't have any money right now.

56
00:05:39,339 --> 00:05:42,174
If I find a single penny
in this dump, you're dead.

57
00:05:44,553 --> 00:05:48,139
I'm going to teach you a lesson!

58
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,520
Get your ass over here!

59
00:05:54,521 --> 00:05:56,021
Damn it.

60
00:05:56,022 --> 00:05:57,231
You think I'm kidding?

61
00:05:57,232 --> 00:05:59,275
- Stop it.
-  Look at me.

62
00:06:02,654 --> 00:06:03,780
Why don't you just…

63
00:06:04,489 --> 00:06:06,074
- Stop it, man.
- Get lost!

64
00:06:07,033 --> 00:06:08,784
Come here. You.

65
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:11,120
What? You found yourself a guy already?

66
00:06:11,121 --> 00:06:13,582
Ha! Seriously, this is ridiculous.

67
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:15,250
Come here.

68
00:06:17,460 --> 00:06:21,338
So you've been giving
all that money to him?

69
00:06:21,339 --> 00:06:23,090
Is that right? Come here.

70
00:06:23,091 --> 00:06:26,260
Come back here.
You don't have money to pay me,

71
00:06:26,261 --> 00:06:28,513
but you've got money for him?

72
00:06:30,432 --> 00:06:33,059
So you've been busy
with your love life, huh?

73
00:06:33,602 --> 00:06:34,977
I said come here!

74
00:06:43,236 --> 00:06:46,531
Wait. Hold on.

75
00:06:50,994 --> 00:06:52,537
I told you to stop it.

76
00:06:54,748 --> 00:06:58,043
I told you to stop it!

77
00:06:58,918 --> 00:07:02,171
I told you to stop.

78
00:07:02,172 --> 00:07:03,757
I told you, didn't I?

79
00:07:33,036 --> 00:07:34,453
Uh…

80
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:41,670
Uh…

81
00:07:42,504 --> 00:07:44,089
Uh…

82
00:07:53,723 --> 00:07:54,933
What are you doing?

83
00:07:55,517 --> 00:07:57,226
I'm calling the cops.

84
00:07:57,227 --> 00:07:58,645
Hey, look at me.

85
00:08:00,188 --> 00:08:02,148
If you hadn't killed this man,

86
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:04,609
I would've been dead.

87
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:11,116
From now on, just do as I say.

88
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:03,667
Get inside.
You're getting rained on.

89
00:09:03,668 --> 00:09:05,045
Oh…

90
00:09:58,723 --> 00:09:59,974
It feels good, doesn't it?

91
00:10:06,231 --> 00:10:07,482
All done.

92
00:10:33,633 --> 00:10:35,885
Well, thank you.

93
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:43,393
For saving me.

94
00:10:53,319 --> 00:10:54,654
Thank you.

95
00:11:38,323 --> 00:11:43,244
THE HUSBAND

96
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:48,124
It's a list of the top sponsors
of this hospital. Have a look.

97
00:11:50,293 --> 00:11:54,547
The other one's the list of people
who made it into the trial.

98
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:57,633
The exact same names.

99
00:11:57,634 --> 00:12:00,470
LEE SEONGUK, PARK DOHYEON
OH MINSEOK

100
00:12:03,264 --> 00:12:05,183
It was all about money.

101
00:12:07,185 --> 00:12:10,730
You didn't lose your spot.
You just never had one to begin with.

102
00:12:13,608 --> 00:12:14,901
But…

103
00:12:16,486 --> 00:12:20,823
Then why did they tell me
it was because I'm an ex-con?

104
00:12:26,204 --> 00:12:27,330
Who said that?

105
00:12:28,665 --> 00:12:31,584
Who told you such a lie and why?

106
00:12:32,502 --> 00:12:35,088
The day Mr. Ha died,
you were in the same elevator.

107
00:12:35,672 --> 00:12:38,549
Plus, your recent contact
with Kim Gyeongae…

108
00:12:41,010 --> 00:12:42,469
Was this all a coincidence?

109
00:12:46,266 --> 00:12:47,350
Answer the question.

110
00:12:50,687 --> 00:12:52,689
When Ms. Kim Gyeongae was in prison,

111
00:12:54,065 --> 00:12:55,733
I handled her psychiatric treatment.

112
00:12:56,859 --> 00:13:00,321
I did it as a volunteer
before joining this hospital.

113
00:13:01,364 --> 00:13:03,574
I met her a few times after her release.

114
00:13:05,201 --> 00:13:07,829
I had meals with her
and checked in on her.

115
00:13:08,621 --> 00:13:10,248
She seemed like a decent person.

116
00:13:10,999 --> 00:13:13,834
I had no idea she'd go
and do something like this.

117
00:13:13,835 --> 00:13:15,127
That's all.

118
00:13:15,128 --> 00:13:17,212
- And that's why you kept this from us?
- Yes.

119
00:13:17,213 --> 00:13:19,047
I didn't want to get involved.

120
00:13:19,048 --> 00:13:23,302
When so many coincidences line up,
it means someone is lying.

121
00:13:23,303 --> 00:13:25,972
Then go find out who's lying.

122
00:13:28,516 --> 00:13:29,517
And next time,

123
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:32,978
bring me evidence, not accusations.

124
00:13:43,698 --> 00:13:44,699
Yeah.

125
00:13:45,199 --> 00:13:46,200
What?

126
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,410
Right now?

127
00:13:48,411 --> 00:13:49,412
Got it.

128
00:13:50,663 --> 00:13:52,873
Let's continue another time.

129
00:13:52,874 --> 00:13:55,043
For now, get yourself to safety.

130
00:13:57,003 --> 00:13:59,129
Noh Manhui is on the way to the hospital.

131
00:14:02,425 --> 00:14:04,469
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

132
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:20,818
Yeah, Detective Jang.

133
00:14:23,112 --> 00:14:24,155
What?

134
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:35,290
INCOMING CALL
HUSBAND

135
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:46,802
Ms. Ko.

136
00:14:48,638 --> 00:14:49,972
It's been a while.

137
00:14:51,933 --> 00:14:53,142
Where's Mr. Kang?

138
00:14:55,937 --> 00:14:57,145
MISSED CALL

139
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:05,904
Don't move, okay?

140
00:15:09,492 --> 00:15:10,743
I said don't move!

141
00:15:25,508 --> 00:15:27,969
I said don't move.

142
00:15:35,935 --> 00:15:36,936
Are you all right?

143
00:15:37,603 --> 00:15:39,104
Honey?

144
00:15:48,072 --> 00:15:49,281
Stay right here.

145
00:15:49,282 --> 00:15:50,740
No! Don't go out there, honey!

146
00:16:42,835 --> 00:16:43,836
Ms. Ko!

147
00:16:44,837 --> 00:16:46,130
- Are you okay?
- Uh…

148
00:16:47,006 --> 00:16:48,506
He went that way.

149
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:50,008
- Go, get after him!
- On it.

150
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,763
Send medical assistance
to the basement stairwell.

151
00:17:04,774 --> 00:17:05,983
Excuse me.

152
00:17:06,651 --> 00:17:07,652
Excuse me!

153
00:17:08,152 --> 00:17:10,196
Is something going on outside?

154
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:16,035
Excuse me!
I said, is something going on out there?

155
00:17:17,536 --> 00:17:19,205
Ms. Ko, take deep breaths.

156
00:17:20,498 --> 00:17:22,291
Hold on.

157
00:17:23,334 --> 00:17:24,417
What happened to her?

158
00:17:24,418 --> 00:17:27,587
We found her in the basement parking.
She's in severe hyperventilation.

159
00:17:27,588 --> 00:17:30,590
I'll go with you. You're fine, Seyun.

160
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:32,760
Just breathe. Slowly. Inhale…

161
00:18:36,407 --> 00:18:38,826
Hey, boss. Guess what?

162
00:18:40,244 --> 00:18:41,746
This is all your fault.

163
00:18:42,413 --> 00:18:44,080
If you…

164
00:18:44,081 --> 00:18:46,124
…had just given me the money you promised,

165
00:18:46,125 --> 00:18:47,626
none of this would be happening.

166
00:18:47,627 --> 00:18:49,086
Who put you up to it?

167
00:18:50,921 --> 00:18:51,922
Who…

168
00:18:53,424 --> 00:18:55,926
Who ordered you to kidnap my wife?

169
00:18:56,510 --> 00:18:57,553
Ah.

170
00:18:58,554 --> 00:19:00,181
That's what you want to know.

171
00:19:01,474 --> 00:19:02,516
That's too bad.

172
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:05,728
You got it all wrong.

173
00:19:09,148 --> 00:19:10,732
Look, you got it all wrong.

174
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:13,277
What?

175
00:19:15,196 --> 00:19:16,781
I wasn't after your wife.

176
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:22,870
Hey, it was you.

177
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:30,086
You're the one I was going to kill.

178
00:19:31,337 --> 00:19:32,963
What are you talking about?

179
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:34,674
Me…

180
00:19:37,218 --> 00:19:40,930
On whose orders? And why?

181
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,851
Does it really matter?
You're going to die either way.

182
00:19:51,399 --> 00:19:52,942
So will your wife.

183
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:55,610
What?

184
00:19:55,611 --> 00:19:57,822
Your wife.

185
00:19:58,322 --> 00:20:01,074
They're going to kill her.

186
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:02,993
They've already tried once.

187
00:20:03,786 --> 00:20:04,995
Someone tried to kill her?

188
00:20:05,705 --> 00:20:07,581
They ordered Dr. Ha Jeongsoo…

189
00:20:09,625 --> 00:20:11,419
to kill your wife.

190
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:16,256
And how do you know that?

191
00:20:16,257 --> 00:20:18,050
Because I saved her.

192
00:20:30,146 --> 00:20:32,148
But they'll try to kill her again.

193
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:03,179
Thanks.

194
00:21:07,099 --> 00:21:09,059
It's a sedative.
You should feel better soon.

195
00:21:27,912 --> 00:21:30,873
LAW ENFORCEMENT

196
00:21:35,461 --> 00:21:37,087
Mr. Kang, are you okay?

197
00:21:37,838 --> 00:21:38,922
Yeah, I'm fine.

198
00:21:38,923 --> 00:21:41,634
You can't just go after him
by yourself like that.

199
00:21:44,929 --> 00:21:50,434
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

200
00:22:07,243 --> 00:22:09,245
Excuse me, nurse.
What's going on out there?

201
00:22:09,745 --> 00:22:11,788
- I'm here to change your IV bag.
- Yeah, okay,

202
00:22:11,789 --> 00:22:14,582
but is something going on outside?

203
00:22:14,583 --> 00:22:15,875
I'm talking to you.

204
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:17,878
- Why won't you answer me?
- Please don't move.

205
00:22:18,838 --> 00:22:20,381
Your husband was here earlier.

206
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:39,692
-  Chiung.
- Hey.

207
00:22:40,276 --> 00:22:41,609
How's Seyun?

208
00:22:41,610 --> 00:22:43,236
Sedated for now.

209
00:22:43,237 --> 00:22:44,405
It's acute stress.

210
00:22:45,906 --> 00:22:49,243
Her body reacted since it was
similar to the trauma she suffered before.

211
00:22:50,411 --> 00:22:51,619
How are you holding up?

212
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:52,663
Yeah, I'm fine.

213
00:22:55,207 --> 00:22:56,500
Director Ko's inside.

214
00:22:58,085 --> 00:22:59,420
Oh, okay. Thanks a lot.

215
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:40,544
What did she do to deserve this?

216
00:23:41,587 --> 00:23:44,089
What are those damn cops doing?

217
00:23:45,466 --> 00:23:46,549
What?

218
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:48,885
You still suspect me?

219
00:23:48,886 --> 00:23:51,512
You still think I tried to have
my own daughter kidnapped

220
00:23:51,513 --> 00:23:53,223
and that woman killed?

221
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:59,020
I don't even want to imagine
that you'd do such a thing to Seyun.

222
00:23:59,021 --> 00:24:00,314
So…

223
00:24:01,440 --> 00:24:03,691
let's be honest with each other.

224
00:24:03,692 --> 00:24:07,321
I can't just stand by
and watch Seyun face danger anymore.

225
00:24:08,405 --> 00:24:09,490
Kim Gyeongae…

226
00:24:12,117 --> 00:24:13,702
You knew about her, didn't you?

227
00:24:16,664 --> 00:24:19,458
Yes, I've seen her before.

228
00:24:20,668 --> 00:24:24,504
I met her when she came in to apply,

229
00:24:24,505 --> 00:24:26,090
with that damn husband of hers.

230
00:24:26,840 --> 00:24:27,925
Kim Gyeongae…

231
00:24:29,468 --> 00:24:31,886
I heard she was screened out
because she's an ex-con.

232
00:24:31,887 --> 00:24:33,430
Is that true?

233
00:24:34,974 --> 00:24:36,349
Who on earth told you that?

234
00:24:36,350 --> 00:24:37,934
Am I wrong?

235
00:24:37,935 --> 00:24:40,270
How the hell would I know
if that woman's an ex-con?

236
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:43,065
That's not on her application.

237
00:24:44,525 --> 00:24:46,777
So she dared to kidnap my daughter

238
00:24:47,361 --> 00:24:49,863
because she wasn't selected
for my project?

239
00:24:51,949 --> 00:24:53,033
I see.

240
00:24:53,951 --> 00:24:55,077
But you know,

241
00:24:56,412 --> 00:24:59,164
that might actually be where it all began.

242
00:25:00,958 --> 00:25:02,042
What?

243
00:25:03,085 --> 00:25:05,170
Because it wasn't fair.

244
00:25:06,714 --> 00:25:09,883
You went on about hope and excitement.

245
00:25:10,759 --> 00:25:13,762
And who gets to enjoy them
all came down to money, didn't it?

246
00:25:14,388 --> 00:25:16,473
That's not how I see it.

247
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:19,184
Donations fund our research,

248
00:25:19,810 --> 00:25:21,478
which saves future patients.

249
00:25:22,396 --> 00:25:25,816
That woman was denied
the opportunity to save her own life.

250
00:25:26,942 --> 00:25:29,069
We can't save every patient.

251
00:25:30,362 --> 00:25:32,281
I opted for the best option…

252
00:25:34,116 --> 00:25:36,118
for a better future.

253
00:25:38,662 --> 00:25:39,663
And I know…

254
00:25:41,623 --> 00:25:43,332
my decision was the right one.

255
00:25:43,333 --> 00:25:46,294
It's that greed of yours
that dragged us into this mess.

256
00:25:46,295 --> 00:25:47,713
I hope you know that.

257
00:25:52,051 --> 00:25:53,052
Father.

258
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:58,307
Besides you, me, and Dr. Ha,

259
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:02,770
who else knows about the hospital

260
00:26:03,812 --> 00:26:05,147
using fetal stem cell samples?

261
00:26:37,805 --> 00:26:39,555
SEONGJIN POLICE
DETECTIVE JANG DOSIK

262
00:26:58,117 --> 00:26:59,326
Long time no see.

263
00:26:59,827 --> 00:27:00,828
How have you been?

264
00:27:06,416 --> 00:27:08,377
But where are you off to in such a hurry,

265
00:27:09,628 --> 00:27:10,629
Dr. Cha Myeonghui?

266
00:27:16,635 --> 00:27:20,055
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER

267
00:27:52,629 --> 00:27:54,381
Yes?

268
00:27:58,093 --> 00:27:59,136
Are you doing okay?

269
00:28:01,972 --> 00:28:03,472
You need to take it easy.

270
00:28:07,060 --> 00:28:08,604
You look worse than I do.

271
00:28:13,275 --> 00:28:15,903
You shouldn't have gone
after him like that. He's dangerous.

272
00:28:19,907 --> 00:28:22,868
Well, you're
not the type to listen, anyway.

273
00:28:33,211 --> 00:28:34,922
Anything else you want to tell me?

274
00:28:37,966 --> 00:28:39,051
Yeah, there is.

275
00:28:44,723 --> 00:28:45,724
What is it?

276
00:28:46,350 --> 00:28:48,810
I thought it was about time you knew.

277
00:28:50,687 --> 00:28:52,397
About our spinal cord project.

278
00:28:54,149 --> 00:28:55,984
It was problematic from the beginning.

279
00:28:58,111 --> 00:28:59,404
What do you mean?

280
00:29:00,030 --> 00:29:02,532
The selection for the clinical trial…

281
00:29:03,700 --> 00:29:05,160
It wasn't made fairly.

282
00:29:06,703 --> 00:29:10,414
The spots were reserved
for the top donors from the get-go.

283
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:11,416
What?

284
00:29:12,834 --> 00:29:14,169
What are you talking about?

285
00:29:14,795 --> 00:29:17,965
The stem cells we were using in
our procedures weren't the approved ones.

286
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:21,176
They were illegally sourced
fetal stem cells.

287
00:29:26,056 --> 00:29:27,391
There's no way.

288
00:29:32,521 --> 00:29:34,564
Who made those decisions?

289
00:29:40,070 --> 00:29:42,739
You see, I thought your father

290
00:29:43,824 --> 00:29:46,326
had something to do with this.

291
00:29:47,411 --> 00:29:49,788
That's why I asked you
to look for those files.

292
00:29:53,792 --> 00:29:57,254
Kim Gyeongae was one
of the applicants who didn't make the cut.

293
00:29:58,630 --> 00:30:00,590
She never stood a chance to begin with.

294
00:30:02,759 --> 00:30:05,178
So is that why all of this is happening?

295
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:08,306
Because of my dad?

296
00:30:11,309 --> 00:30:14,228
It's true that your father
made his share of mistakes,

297
00:30:14,229 --> 00:30:18,025
but he wasn't behind your kidnapping.
I've confirmed that myself.

298
00:30:42,966 --> 00:30:44,468
Did you get any sleep last night?

299
00:30:46,511 --> 00:30:49,556
What about you?
It looked like you didn't sleep a wink.

300
00:30:51,516 --> 00:30:52,893
Gosh.

301
00:30:53,935 --> 00:30:55,062
Stop worrying so much.

302
00:30:56,313 --> 00:30:59,608
I've been checking in on Seyun at work,

303
00:31:00,275 --> 00:31:01,985
and Taeju is with her.

304
00:31:02,611 --> 00:31:03,612
You're right.

305
00:31:05,405 --> 00:31:08,158
You have to stay strong
at times like this.

306
00:31:08,784 --> 00:31:10,452
HAIR COLLAGEN 3270

307
00:31:12,788 --> 00:31:13,789
Gosh.

308
00:31:14,414 --> 00:31:17,583
I've been so out of it
that I completely forgot to take this.

309
00:31:17,584 --> 00:31:21,170
No patient wants a hospital director
who looks more washed out than they do.

310
00:31:21,171 --> 00:31:23,214
Take one every day. Don't forget.

311
00:31:25,175 --> 00:31:29,845
You know, I've noticed
that taking this makes a big difference.

312
00:31:32,849 --> 00:31:34,892
It's also supposed
to be good for your skin.

313
00:31:34,893 --> 00:31:36,560
You should take one too.

314
00:31:36,561 --> 00:31:38,271
- Shall I?
- Mmm.

315
00:31:46,863 --> 00:31:48,865
It already feels good.

316
00:31:50,033 --> 00:31:51,409
Things will get better in time.

317
00:31:52,869 --> 00:31:54,246
I hope so.

318
00:32:11,388 --> 00:32:13,807
Oh, Dr. Kang.
Are you hurt at all from yesterday?

319
00:32:14,391 --> 00:32:17,060
No, I'm fine. But what's going on?

320
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:19,396
Ms. Cha Myeonghui has fled.

321
00:32:20,147 --> 00:32:21,814
What do you mean, she's fled?

322
00:32:21,815 --> 00:32:24,400
You see, she was the last person
Mr. Ha was with

323
00:32:24,401 --> 00:32:26,778
on the day he died,
which makes her a prime suspect.

324
00:32:27,737 --> 00:32:28,821
Myeonghui?

325
00:32:28,822 --> 00:32:31,323
She's known Kim Gyeongae
since she was in prison.

326
00:32:31,324 --> 00:32:34,411
It seems like they've been
in touch after her release too.

327
00:32:35,078 --> 00:32:36,955
Myeonghui was acquainted

328
00:32:37,873 --> 00:32:40,457
with Kim Gyeongae?

329
00:32:40,458 --> 00:32:43,628
Yes, we went to her house
with an arrest warrant,

330
00:32:44,212 --> 00:32:46,756
but she'd already packed up
and disappeared.

331
00:33:24,669 --> 00:33:26,045
BEHAVIORAL HEALTH
CONSULTATION ROOM

332
00:33:35,388 --> 00:33:36,806
Come on in, Taeju.

333
00:33:46,858 --> 00:33:47,984
Are you okay?

334
00:33:50,111 --> 00:33:51,112
No.

335
00:33:56,243 --> 00:33:58,954
Sounds like the talk didn't go so well.

336
00:34:04,125 --> 00:34:07,003
I thought we'd been using
adult stem cells.

337
00:34:09,047 --> 00:34:10,298
But we weren't.

338
00:34:12,926 --> 00:34:14,761
They were fetal stem cells.

339
00:34:16,346 --> 00:34:18,181
Fetal stem cells?

340
00:34:20,100 --> 00:34:21,101
Yes.

341
00:34:22,227 --> 00:34:24,062
So that's what it was.

342
00:34:26,147 --> 00:34:27,148
Have you

343
00:34:27,899 --> 00:34:29,442
told anyone else about it?

344
00:34:32,279 --> 00:34:33,321
No, not yet.

345
00:34:35,490 --> 00:34:37,491
Sorry for showing up out of the blue.

346
00:34:37,492 --> 00:34:40,328
I had nowhere else
to sort my thoughts out.

347
00:34:41,746 --> 00:34:42,831
No, it's good.

348
00:34:43,540 --> 00:34:44,791
I'm glad you came.

349
00:34:46,501 --> 00:34:48,503
I should tell Seyun, shouldn't I?

350
00:34:50,588 --> 00:34:51,589
Taeju.

351
00:34:54,050 --> 00:34:55,176
Uh…

352
00:34:57,429 --> 00:34:59,848
You're still processing this right now.

353
00:35:01,057 --> 00:35:02,642
Do you think Seyun would be

354
00:35:03,560 --> 00:35:06,646
able to handle this if you told her now?

355
00:35:08,189 --> 00:35:09,733
It'll just cause misunderstandings.

356
00:35:11,568 --> 00:35:14,070
You may not have known about it,
but you've been using

357
00:35:15,405 --> 00:35:18,533
illegal material in your procedures.
That much is true.

358
00:35:26,875 --> 00:35:28,793
It's okay. It happens.

359
00:35:35,008 --> 00:35:36,384
It's okay, Taeju.

360
00:35:39,763 --> 00:35:40,930
Don't you worry.

361
00:35:41,806 --> 00:35:43,058
This isn't the end.

362
00:35:46,102 --> 00:35:47,145
I should be going.

363
00:35:50,231 --> 00:35:51,900
Thank you for hearing me out.

364
00:35:53,276 --> 00:35:54,736
Taeju.

365
00:35:58,281 --> 00:36:00,240
Now's not the time.

366
00:36:00,241 --> 00:36:01,451
You must not tell her.

367
00:36:07,165 --> 00:36:08,333
Never.

368
00:36:11,628 --> 00:36:13,629
She knew all about it,

369
00:36:13,630 --> 00:36:15,215
even before I told her.

370
00:36:40,115 --> 00:36:43,867
Honestly, every time I saw you people,
I kept thinking, "Why would they do this?"

371
00:36:43,868 --> 00:36:45,453
"Just why?"

372
00:36:47,706 --> 00:36:50,917
"Why did they do this to my wife?
Why did they kidnap her?"

373
00:36:57,590 --> 00:37:00,176
But to find out
that you were after me, not my wife…

374
00:37:01,469 --> 00:37:02,595
That was kind of a shock.

375
00:37:06,057 --> 00:37:08,560
How do you know that? Who told you?

376
00:37:09,269 --> 00:37:10,395
Noh Manhui.

377
00:37:11,187 --> 00:37:12,605
Your husband, Noh Manhui.

378
00:37:14,357 --> 00:37:16,650
You met my husband?

379
00:37:16,651 --> 00:37:19,778
He seemed quite shocked
when I told him Dr. Ha tried to kill you.

380
00:37:19,779 --> 00:37:21,865
He was very worried about you.

381
00:37:23,199 --> 00:37:24,200
So now…

382
00:37:26,202 --> 00:37:27,662
your husband should know as well.

383
00:37:30,248 --> 00:37:32,751
That you were both used and tossed aside.

384
00:37:37,922 --> 00:37:42,426
Right before he died,
Dr. Ha met Myeonghui in the elevator.

385
00:37:42,427 --> 00:37:44,344
After they talked,

386
00:37:44,345 --> 00:37:47,682
he changed his destination,
and died moments later.

387
00:37:49,726 --> 00:37:52,978
Dr. Cha was there with him?

388
00:37:52,979 --> 00:37:54,062
Why?

389
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:57,150
Why are you so surprised
that those two ran into each other?

390
00:38:01,613 --> 00:38:03,698
I've been thinking about it.

391
00:38:06,493 --> 00:38:07,994
Myeonghui was in the know as well.

392
00:38:08,745 --> 00:38:09,746
About what?

393
00:38:11,498 --> 00:38:13,583
The fetal stem cells.

394
00:38:18,505 --> 00:38:19,923
Was it Dr. Cha?

395
00:38:22,133 --> 00:38:24,844
The one who lied to you
that your prior got you rejected?

396
00:38:27,055 --> 00:38:29,932
I mean, you two
have been in touch all along,

397
00:38:29,933 --> 00:38:31,810
since back when you were in prison.

398
00:38:33,102 --> 00:38:36,689
Yeah, so what?
I mean, what's so wrong about that?

399
00:38:39,025 --> 00:38:40,360
Ah.

400
00:38:41,194 --> 00:38:42,862
You must think

401
00:38:43,822 --> 00:38:46,866
you're in a different league
than a criminal like me, don't you?

402
00:38:47,951 --> 00:38:49,577
But guess what?

403
00:38:50,370 --> 00:38:54,915
You're the one who exploited
those dead babies

404
00:38:54,916 --> 00:38:57,043
for your benefit, not me.

405
00:38:59,462 --> 00:39:00,630
All I wanted…

406
00:39:01,589 --> 00:39:02,714
I…

407
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:04,342
I just wanted to live.

408
00:39:07,136 --> 00:39:08,805
It can't be Dr. Cha.

409
00:39:10,139 --> 00:39:13,434
She always told me to never give up.

410
00:39:13,935 --> 00:39:15,978
She said in that clinical trial,

411
00:39:15,979 --> 00:39:20,441
they could make brand-new nerves
and put them into me.

412
00:39:21,025 --> 00:39:22,110
She said she'd help me.

413
00:39:22,735 --> 00:39:26,155
She told you that
they'd give you new nerves?

414
00:39:28,449 --> 00:39:31,077
Dr. Cha said that to you?
She's a psychiatrist.

415
00:39:33,454 --> 00:39:38,126
I mean, how could she possibly
help you in that situation?

416
00:39:41,546 --> 00:39:42,881
Myeonghui…

417
00:39:47,510 --> 00:39:50,513
introduced you to someone, didn't she?

418
00:39:53,182 --> 00:39:56,685
I don't even know
what you're talking about.

419
00:39:56,686 --> 00:39:57,979
What are you even saying?

420
00:39:59,856 --> 00:40:02,859
She's gone off the grid.
What was she so afraid of?

421
00:40:04,485 --> 00:40:08,740
Your husband ran away, Dr. Ha is dead,
and Myeonghui's disappeared.

422
00:40:11,242 --> 00:40:12,327
So now…

423
00:40:14,621 --> 00:40:16,080
you're all by yourself.

424
00:40:24,631 --> 00:40:27,257
They're all the same.

425
00:40:27,258 --> 00:40:29,928
They all use me and just toss me aside.

426
00:40:34,098 --> 00:40:37,101
WING 102 ROOM 07
KIM G.A

427
00:41:18,351 --> 00:41:20,603
FUND DONATION AGREEMENT,
CLINICAL TRIAL APPLICATION

428
00:41:22,063 --> 00:41:23,313
100 MILLION WON

429
00:41:23,314 --> 00:41:26,025
OH MINSEOK
ACCEPTED

430
00:41:27,318 --> 00:41:28,485
550 MILLION WON

431
00:41:28,486 --> 00:41:30,862
LEE SEONGUK
ACCEPTED

432
00:41:32,448 --> 00:41:33,449
270 MILLION WON

433
00:41:34,367 --> 00:41:36,828
PARK DOHYEON
ACCEPTED

434
00:41:38,705 --> 00:41:40,498
KIM JEONGHUI
190 MILLION WON

435
00:41:47,255 --> 00:41:50,924
KIM GYEONGAE
SCREENED OUT

436
00:41:50,925 --> 00:41:52,844
SCREENED OUT

437
00:41:54,595 --> 00:41:55,972
What are you doing here?

438
00:42:01,728 --> 00:42:04,147
Why are you in your father's study?

439
00:42:06,524 --> 00:42:08,026
Mom, did you know about this?

440
00:42:09,110 --> 00:42:10,778
About what, dear?

441
00:42:12,321 --> 00:42:13,823
About what Dad did.

442
00:42:15,241 --> 00:42:17,869
What are you talking about?

443
00:42:21,414 --> 00:42:23,750
Never mind. It's nothing.
Don't worry about it.

444
00:42:26,419 --> 00:42:27,754
Wait, Seyun?

445
00:42:40,391 --> 00:42:41,726
Seyun.

446
00:42:51,402 --> 00:42:54,238
WOORI TOGETHER MEDICAL CENTER
FUND DONATION AGREEMENT

447
00:43:00,453 --> 00:43:02,455
It was just as you said.

448
00:43:04,373 --> 00:43:05,958
Why didn't you tell me?

449
00:43:07,585 --> 00:43:09,420
Do I not deserve to know?

450
00:43:15,927 --> 00:43:18,346
I had no idea what my dad had done.

451
00:43:21,099 --> 00:43:23,101
But you knew all along.

452
00:43:24,352 --> 00:43:26,020
Why did you make me out to be a fool?

453
00:43:27,313 --> 00:43:28,898
It's not like that, Seyun.

454
00:43:30,066 --> 00:43:31,067
Then what is it?

455
00:43:35,696 --> 00:43:37,406
I just felt like I shouldn't tell you.

456
00:43:38,282 --> 00:43:39,283
Why not?

457
00:43:43,121 --> 00:43:44,872
Why did you think you shouldn't tell me?

458
00:43:45,456 --> 00:43:46,457
Why?

459
00:43:56,342 --> 00:43:57,385
Hold on.

460
00:44:00,096 --> 00:44:01,264
That day…

461
00:44:02,890 --> 00:44:04,308
The day we lost Hayun.

462
00:44:05,268 --> 00:44:06,853
Were you late because…

463
00:44:11,149 --> 00:44:14,902
The patients consented to the procedure
thinking it was their own stem cells.

464
00:44:15,695 --> 00:44:17,779
This is completely illegal, Father.

465
00:44:17,780 --> 00:44:19,699
Those illegal procedures

466
00:44:20,575 --> 00:44:23,661
helped people regain movement
and stand on their own two feet.

467
00:44:24,704 --> 00:44:27,582
They're hopeful
and excited about the future.

468
00:44:28,666 --> 00:44:30,209
That is not hope.

469
00:44:33,171 --> 00:44:36,757
Any hope that's built on a lie
is bound to fall apart.

470
00:44:38,009 --> 00:44:40,011
Please count me out of this project.

471
00:44:46,726 --> 00:44:48,060
What about Seyun?

472
00:44:50,897 --> 00:44:52,481
What will you do about her?

473
00:44:53,691 --> 00:44:55,359
Whether you do the surgery or not,

474
00:44:56,235 --> 00:44:57,695
that's your call.

475
00:44:59,280 --> 00:45:02,033
But it won't be you

476
00:45:03,034 --> 00:45:04,285
who pays the price.

477
00:45:05,161 --> 00:45:06,746
It will be Seyun.

478
00:45:17,465 --> 00:45:18,549
Dr. Kang.

479
00:45:20,801 --> 00:45:22,220
I mean, Taeju.

480
00:45:23,346 --> 00:45:25,097
Do you think I've never felt that way?

481
00:45:26,432 --> 00:45:28,016
I've been there.

482
00:45:28,017 --> 00:45:31,061
But I had a family to protect.

483
00:45:31,062 --> 00:45:33,231
I just had to suck it up.

484
00:45:33,814 --> 00:45:36,651
That's how I've kept myself going.

485
00:45:41,113 --> 00:45:42,448
Your heart,

486
00:45:43,491 --> 00:45:44,825
your values, your morals…

487
00:45:45,326 --> 00:45:46,869
Just put them all aside.

488
00:45:48,371 --> 00:45:50,289
Don't let Seyun catch on.

489
00:45:50,873 --> 00:45:53,584
It'd only hurt her, all right?

490
00:45:54,627 --> 00:45:55,753
If you

491
00:45:57,171 --> 00:46:00,508
really love her, please.

492
00:46:46,012 --> 00:46:47,179
You're home.

493
00:46:49,307 --> 00:46:51,225
Where were you all night?

494
00:46:52,101 --> 00:46:53,810
Why are you out here?

495
00:46:53,811 --> 00:46:55,313
You should be in bed.

496
00:46:56,897 --> 00:46:59,024
You've been acting weird lately.

497
00:46:59,025 --> 00:47:01,110
You're always late,
and I can never reach you.

498
00:47:05,448 --> 00:47:06,615
Something came up.

499
00:47:11,329 --> 00:47:12,663
Honey.

500
00:47:14,123 --> 00:47:15,708
Are you hiding something from me?

501
00:47:18,336 --> 00:47:19,503
I'm not.

502
00:47:22,631 --> 00:47:24,216
You sure there's nothing going on?

503
00:47:25,968 --> 00:47:26,969
I'm sure.

504
00:47:29,513 --> 00:47:30,931
Fine.

505
00:47:33,893 --> 00:47:35,227
Listen.

506
00:47:35,978 --> 00:47:37,313
I'm your wife.

507
00:47:38,773 --> 00:47:42,526
You have to tell me
if there is something going on.

508
00:47:43,194 --> 00:47:46,739
I can tell you're having a hard time,
but you won't say anything.

509
00:47:59,585 --> 00:48:00,920
Where's your wedding ring?

510
00:48:03,047 --> 00:48:06,425
I took it off before surgery.
I probably left it in the office.

511
00:48:10,513 --> 00:48:12,515
- I'm going to turn in.
- All right.

512
00:48:19,939 --> 00:48:21,607
Daddy.

513
00:48:22,400 --> 00:48:23,566
Oh, hey, Hayun.

514
00:48:23,567 --> 00:48:25,110
My goodness.

515
00:48:25,111 --> 00:48:27,320
What are you doing up so late?

516
00:48:27,321 --> 00:48:28,905
Waiting for you, Daddy.

517
00:48:28,906 --> 00:48:30,907
Goodness, did you?

518
00:48:30,908 --> 00:48:33,119
My sweet little girl.

519
00:48:42,336 --> 00:48:43,962
HOSPITAL DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

520
00:48:43,963 --> 00:48:45,131
Your heart…

521
00:48:46,549 --> 00:48:48,092
Just put them all aside.

522
00:48:49,093 --> 00:48:52,638
If you really love her, please.

523
00:49:42,480 --> 00:49:46,149
Dr. Ko, your granddaughter has
just been brought into the ER.

524
00:49:46,150 --> 00:49:48,568
- What? Hayun is here?
- Yes.

525
00:49:48,569 --> 00:49:49,904
How bad is it?

526
00:49:50,571 --> 00:49:52,697
It looks like she has
a cervical spine injury.

527
00:49:52,698 --> 00:49:54,116
She needs emergency surgery.

528
00:49:54,617 --> 00:49:57,495
Ms. Ko is looking for Dr. Kang.

529
00:49:58,287 --> 00:50:00,247
Should I give him a call?

530
00:50:03,959 --> 00:50:04,960
Dr. Ko?

531
00:50:06,629 --> 00:50:08,339
He's connecting nerve ends right now.

532
00:50:09,340 --> 00:50:12,510
If he stops now,
the patient will never stand again.

533
00:50:14,345 --> 00:50:16,430
Tell Dr. Park to take over
the surgery for now.

534
00:50:17,306 --> 00:50:20,976
I'll talk to Dr. Kang
when he's done with this.

535
00:50:24,104 --> 00:50:25,522
Wait, Doctor.

536
00:50:25,523 --> 00:50:27,733
Can you wait until Dr. Kang gets here?

537
00:50:28,400 --> 00:50:29,734
We don't have time.

538
00:50:29,735 --> 00:50:30,985
We'll try our best.

539
00:50:30,986 --> 00:50:33,154
Ms. Ko. I have to ask you
to wait out here.

540
00:50:33,155 --> 00:50:34,822
CALLING
HUSBAND

541
00:50:36,283 --> 00:50:38,701
Come on, honey, pick up.

542
00:50:38,702 --> 00:50:40,829
Please. Hayun is…

543
00:50:42,498 --> 00:50:46,125
Where is he? Why won't he pick up?

544
00:50:47,586 --> 00:50:49,255
Where on earth is he?

545
00:50:50,005 --> 00:50:51,714
Okay, can you wrap this up for me?

546
00:50:51,715 --> 00:50:52,800
- Okay.
- Okay.

547
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:13,653
She's flatlining!

548
00:51:32,381 --> 00:51:33,465
Dr. Kang.

549
00:51:43,225 --> 00:51:44,893
Where have you been?

550
00:51:58,824 --> 00:52:02,202
I said, where have you been?

551
00:52:08,917 --> 00:52:10,919
Where have you been?

552
00:52:15,299 --> 00:52:18,135
Answer me!

553
00:52:22,097 --> 00:52:23,432
Why?

554
00:52:27,102 --> 00:52:30,022
Why have you carried
that burden all by yourself?

555
00:52:34,068 --> 00:52:35,944
I had no idea,

556
00:52:36,987 --> 00:52:38,906
so I just kept blaming you.

557
00:52:39,573 --> 00:52:40,948
Asking where you were,

558
00:52:40,949 --> 00:52:43,661
why you never came,
and saying it was all your fault.

559
00:52:57,341 --> 00:53:00,844
It must've been just as hard on you
after we lost Hayun.

560
00:53:03,138 --> 00:53:05,640
Why you had changed so much

561
00:53:05,641 --> 00:53:07,726
and why you'd become so silent…

562
00:53:09,019 --> 00:53:10,854
I didn't even try to understand.

563
00:53:11,730 --> 00:53:13,774
I just kept pushing you
to answer my questions,

564
00:53:14,566 --> 00:53:16,735
without ever trying to hear you out.

565
00:53:22,366 --> 00:53:24,659
You should've told me.

566
00:53:24,660 --> 00:53:26,870
Why couldn't you just tell me?

567
00:53:27,788 --> 00:53:30,833
I had no idea,
so all I could do was resent you.

568
00:53:33,711 --> 00:53:35,129
I was afraid…

569
00:53:38,757 --> 00:53:40,259
that you'd break down.

570
00:53:42,302 --> 00:53:43,303
What?

571
00:53:46,265 --> 00:53:50,853
Hayun is already gone, and I thought
the truth would push you over the edge.

572
00:53:54,231 --> 00:53:55,232
That's

573
00:53:57,025 --> 00:53:58,026
what I was…

574
00:54:01,113 --> 00:54:02,614
so scared of.

575
00:54:12,666 --> 00:54:14,792
I'm okay with you resenting me.

576
00:54:14,793 --> 00:54:16,503
Even if you resented me and blamed me,

577
00:54:17,588 --> 00:54:19,423
I'd stay by your side.

578
00:54:21,175 --> 00:54:22,176
But…

579
00:54:23,385 --> 00:54:27,806
if you found out the truth
and broke down, I…

580
00:54:30,601 --> 00:54:31,769
I thought if that happened, I…

581
00:54:35,939 --> 00:54:37,566
I might lose you too.

582
00:54:38,984 --> 00:54:41,152
I was so scared of that.

583
00:54:41,153 --> 00:54:42,154
I'm sorry.

584
00:54:46,742 --> 00:54:49,203
I'm sorry.

585
00:54:52,706 --> 00:54:54,249
I'm so sorry, honey.

586
00:54:58,462 --> 00:55:01,924
It must have been so hard.

587
00:55:02,716 --> 00:55:05,886
You must've been living in hell, honey.

588
00:55:07,971 --> 00:55:08,972
No.

589
00:55:09,765 --> 00:55:11,099
I'm sorry.

590
00:55:11,642 --> 00:55:13,059
I'm so sorry.

591
00:55:13,060 --> 00:55:16,395
I'm sorry, honey.
You can tell me anything now, okay?

592
00:55:16,396 --> 00:55:18,899
Don't keep it all bottled up inside!

593
00:55:22,736 --> 00:55:23,987
Seyun.

594
00:55:26,281 --> 00:55:28,408
They were never after you.

595
00:55:29,785 --> 00:55:31,370
What are you talking about?

596
00:55:32,329 --> 00:55:33,830
They were after me.

597
00:55:35,582 --> 00:55:37,125
I'm the one they wanted to kill.

598
00:56:07,573 --> 00:56:08,656
Yeah.

599
00:57:49,800 --> 00:57:51,926
Who are you?

600
00:57:51,927 --> 00:57:54,095
Wait, who the hell are you?

601
00:57:55,389 --> 00:57:56,431
Hold on.

602
00:57:57,391 --> 00:58:00,811
You had me do all your dirty work,
and now you feign ignorance?

603
00:58:02,062 --> 00:58:03,689
What the hell are you talking about?

604
00:58:04,815 --> 00:58:06,233
I heard about it all.

605
00:58:07,067 --> 00:58:10,070
You tried to kill my wife, didn't you?

606
00:58:14,491 --> 00:58:15,909
So what now?

607
00:58:17,786 --> 00:58:19,955
Who will save your wife if I die?

608
00:58:24,501 --> 00:58:27,337
Who else do you think
will save your wife?

609
00:58:42,686 --> 00:58:47,606
THE HUSBAND

610
00:59:27,647 --> 00:59:31,567
They offered to operate on her
if you killed me.

611
00:59:31,568 --> 00:59:34,236
I'll operate on her.
But I have one condition.

612
00:59:34,237 --> 00:59:36,865
Could Myeonghui really pull this off
all on her own?

613
00:59:37,449 --> 00:59:41,077
What I'll say then is up to you, isn't it?

614
00:59:41,703 --> 00:59:44,663
Kang Taeju.
You've been the problem all along.

615
00:59:44,664 --> 00:59:47,792
There are too many things
that can't be undone.

616
00:59:47,793 --> 00:59:50,337
But we have to make right what we can.

617
00:59:51,004 --> 00:59:53,339
Where's my wife?
I know you took her.

618
00:59:53,340 --> 00:59:56,801
My husband will not let you
get away with this.

619
00:59:56,802 --> 00:59:57,927
Keep your word.

620
00:59:57,928 --> 00:59:59,387
I'll do as you say.

621
00:59:59,971 --> 01:00:01,973
Translated by Hyun Sik Yoon
